      "heading": "B - Audience, Section Eight Safe Driving",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B - Audience, Section Eight Safe Driving\n\nThe audience is first-time never-licensed applicants preparing for the regular noncommercial Class C written knowledge test in California, reading at a plain-English level. Section Eight teaches defensive driving only, from scanning and following distance through night and weather hazards, restraints, speed control, emergencies, and distraction; it assumes no prior driving knowledge and carries no prerequisites beyond literacy. Content progresses from watching the road to surviving its hazards and protecting every occupant.\n",
